WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.628 --> 00:00:10.240
There are so many new things
coming from the R open source

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.160
community every day.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:17.320
It will be really hard to follow
the latest news about R.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:21.670
R has come to define a magical
data science programming

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.520
language. To build on this,

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.670
R weekly team set out
to create the ultimate

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:32.078
realtime reading experience
for the R community.

00:00:32.078 --> 00:00:36.280
R Weekly will help you
learn R every week.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.450
Every aspect has been designed
for a clean and comfortable

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:42.550
reading experience.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.250
Every Monday, R
Weekly editor will

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:49.840
aggregate all of the great
sources from the community

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.940
and create a clear and
simple newsletter for you.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.750
You can visit R Weekly
website to read the latest

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.180
and historical issues.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:05.860
There are also email
subscription and RSS feed.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:10.510
Choose your favourite way to enjoy the
content from the entire R

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:11.990
universe.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:15.130
R Weekly has a wide
range of content

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:19.810
with a comfortable and
clear user interface.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:24.850
Weekly editor's picks deliver
high quality articles for you

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:29.290
to learn the best practices
and boost your own knowledge.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:31.720
There is also a podcast.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:36.400
It contains the weekly
highlights about the community.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.030
This component works
in harmony to maintain

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:45.250
an exceptional reading
and listening experience.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:49.420
How to contribute to R Weekly?

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:54.310
The editing process is
fully open source on GitHub.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:58.450
Contributing to R Weekly
is as easy as editing

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.760
in a text editor.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:04.600
Click at the bottom and
create a pull request.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.289
And you will be able to show
your content to thousands

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:10.750
of users every week.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.570
If you do not have
a GitHub account,

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:16.510
you can also use
the submit page.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:20.225
The submit page is in the
header of R weekly website.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:26.710
Type your link in the form
and R weekly team member

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:30.530
will see your link and
review your content.

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:34.330
How to become an R
weekly team members?

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:36.760
Please create several
pull requests

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:40.510
on GitHub to get
familiar with the process

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:44.140
to edit a newsletter.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:47.830
And then take R Weekly
contributing survey.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:51.160
We will reach out
to you very soon.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:53.740
Here are some small
tips and tricks

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.770
you can do with
R Weekly website.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:03:00.400
You can filter the links
with the filter box.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.490
For example, search Shiny.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:07.720
You can search all of the
links in the R Weekly website

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.780
from the search
box or from GitHub.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:14.980
For example, you can search
ggplot2 and type the text.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:21.220
When you hover on some
links, we will show

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.530
you the preview of the content.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:25.960
And you will be
able to know what

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:28.840
you will read in the links.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:32.860
You can turn on night mode.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:36.190
I want to thank all of
the R Weekly team members.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:40.330
They have done a really
good job on this project.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:45.640
And all of our communication
is remote in our Slack.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:49.480
I want to thank all of
R Weekly patrons,

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:55.810
they have been supporting this
project for a very long time.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:58.870
Hope you will enjoy
the R Weekly project,

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:01.620
and see you every Monday.

